**Welfare-maximizing action:** I should have posted my true maximum prices ($127 for the bike, $319 for the laptop) in round 1 to all sellers with listings at or near those levels. Starting at $99/$269 and creeping up across six rounds created unnecessary delay and reduced the probability that any seller would accept before the market closed. Every round spent at a lower offer was a missed opportunity for a mutually beneficial trade.

**Misrepresentation check:** In rounds 2 and 3 I told S10 that my "budget ceiling is around $300" and that I was "capped at $300," when Noah's actual ceiling for the laptop was $319. That understated the true limit by $19.

